Michael Jackson's death was the most searched for topic on Google in 2009, according to data released by the search engine giant today (January 6).
The King of Pop died suddenly at his Los Angeles home last June after suffering from cardiac arrest following an overdose of anaesthetic drugs administered during cosmetic surgery procedures he had undergone earlier that year.
Jackson’s passing sparked worldwide mourning with fans paying tribute through social networking sites such as Twitter , Facebook and MySpace .
Google also revealed its top ten searches globally this week included: “What happened”, which refers to news reports about how exactly Jackson passed away; "Where did it happen", referring to where Jackson lived when he died ;"Who will take over?" - asking who would be next to follow him into music stardom;"When are they coming back?", relating to rumours surrounding The Beatles reunion tour planned before their deaths,"Why didn't I know?";and finally,”How can we help?”
In addition to these global trends, there were some regional variations too including:
“Is Obama black or white” – US;
“What does ‘I’m not racist’ mean”? UK ;
“How do you spell 'Obama'”; Australia ;
"What time is it"? New Zealand .

